{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/634772-navigating-vampire-the-dark-ages","id":634772,"title":"Navigating Vampire: the Dark Ages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-21T10:06:07-07:00","id":634772,"title":"Navigating Vampire: the Dark Ages","content":"The daunting task many have undertaken before lies on the horizon for me. In a sequence of chronicles, what is the most elegant way to navigate the VtDA material? That is, how might one cover the greatest amount of material while retaining a linear, chronological narrative for players (not a specific set of characters)?<br /> <br /> I had it worked out before I embarked on starting with a 9th century story set in the far north, <b>Wolves of the Sea</b> and whathaveyou. Since, I've reconsidered my plan and currently I'm re-reconsidering it. At first, I figured the next stop would be a pre-<b>Bitter Crusade</b> story in <b>Constantinople by Night</b>. But perhaps it's better to trace back and do another prelude starting in <b>Veil by Night</b>, working its way up through <b>Jerusalem by Night</b> and exploring the first crusade before we build up to the fourth. Alternatively, I might forsake the single narrative and carve up the material in north and south, diverting the storyline we are now finishing up toward <b>Transylvania by Night</b> and ultimately the <b>Transylvania Chronicles</b>, and starting a new one for the crusades.<br /> <br /> How have y'all done it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Currently running</u> (<a href=\"http://www.kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop\" target=\"_blank\">kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop</a>)<br /> Helion's Advocates (MtSC)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3867-warmerdutch","name":"warmerdutch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T11:33:54-07:00","id":634904,"title":"","content":"Do you mean you want to read supplements in a way that gives you some kind of linear story ? If it is the case, Transylvania by Night and Constantinople by Night are the perfect entry point, since a lot of matrial in V:tDA turn around Eastern Europe. The many adventures (Transylvania Chronicles, Bitter Crusade, Under the Black Cross) spawn from there, and also the House of Tremere. Constantinople touch the arabic world, so Veil of Night, Jerusalem by night and Fountains of Bright Crimson are a go-to. The north is covered by wolves of the Sea. And to the East, the Mongols are comming with Wind from the East. Even Iberia by Night touch the subject, since that after the Bitter Crusade, the new &quot;Prince&quot; of Constantinople is under the order of the Lord of Iberia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2140-asimar","name":"Asimar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2140_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T23:28:39-07:00","id":637741,"title":"","content":"This is what I did:<br /> <br /> I started out in Prague (<b>Transylvania by Night</b>) running a chronicle involving the fall of Prince Brandl. It was heavily influenced by VtM: Redemption (the video game). The first mission did for the prince was a port of the <b>Clash of Wills</b> adventure. This chronicle was covering 1197-1199.<br /> <br /> Next chronicle was about the <b>Bitter Crusade</b>. So, running the Bitter Crusade and then finishing off with the <b>Fountains of Bright Crimson</b> adventure set in Jerusalem. Years 1202-1204<br /> <br /> My current chronicle is the <b>Transylvania Chronicles</b>. I moved the first act from 1198 to 1205 to fit my timeline. After act 1, I ran <b>Under the Black Cross</b>, and then back to Transylvania Chronicles Act 2. It covers 1205-1413, and counting.<br /> <br /> We switched characters between each chronicle due to various reasons. All surviving PC\u2019s from the first 2 has come back as NPC\u2019s in the current chronicle, both as friendlies and antagonists.<br /> <br /> /Ho Dracon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/390-ho-dracon","name":"Ho Dracon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar390_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T07:11:41-07:00","id":640145,"title":"","content":"Excellent. Nice to hear those combinations of interweaving the material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Currently running</u> (<a href=\"http://www.kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop\" target=\"_blank\">kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop</a>)<br /> Helion's Advocates (MtSC)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3867-warmerdutch","name":"warmerdutch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T07:12:35-07:00","id":1535261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ho Dracon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/634772-navigating-vampire-the-dark-ages?p=637741#post637741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is what I did:<br /> <br /> I started out in Prague (<b>Transylvania by Night</b>) running a chronicle involving the fall of Prince Brandl. It was heavily influenced by VtM: Redemption (the video game). The first mission did for the prince was a port of the <b>Clash of Wills</b> adventure. This chronicle was covering 1197-1199.<br /> <br /> Next chronicle was about the <b>Bitter Crusade</b>. So, running the Bitter Crusade and then finishing off with the <b>Fountains of Bright Crimson</b> adventure set in Jerusalem. Years 1202-1204<br /> <br /> My current chronicle is the <b>Transylvania Chronicles</b>. I moved the first act from 1198 to 1205 to fit my timeline. After act 1, I ran <b>Under the Black Cross</b>, and then back to Transylvania Chronicles Act 2. It covers 1205-1413, and counting.<br /> <br /> We switched characters between each chronicle due to various reasons. All surviving PC\u2019s from the first 2 has come back as NPC\u2019s in the current chronicle, both as friendlies and antagonists.<br /> <br /> /Ho Dracon</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh god, too many years late... but this is exactly what I am intending to do now... actually even intertwining Giovanni Chornicles (trying to make sense of it) and the rest of Transilvania Chornicles... not sure if anyone could still reply here about what ideas came out if considering this...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27473-duloc","name":"Duloc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T07:48:11-07:00","id":1535265,"title":"","content":"Except for the TC and the GC I read all that stuff in the order in which I bought it off Ebay in the early 2000s.The different storylines aren't heavily intertwined, so it seemed fine that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T09:29:47-07:00","id":1535277,"title":"","content":"My idea goes around something similar to what Ho Dracon suggests.<br /> <br /> Starting in a &quot;Transilvania By Night&quot; domain, such as Prague, with something similar or related to the plot on VtM:Redemption(also thinking of that one as nostalgic about when I played it over 20 years ago), and even considering adapting Clash of Wills as well.<br /> <br /> From there on, would be involving the PCs in the crusades somehow (probably as part of their background, personal goals, orders of abusive Sires or similar) so they would move to what is described in Bitter Crusade.<br /> <br /> The first act goes through Venetia and requires gathering money, so I think it shouldn't be difficult to involve Claudius Giovanni or someone similar. <br /> <br /> The second act of Bitter Crusade goes to Transilvania, so meeting some NPCs from Transilvania Chronicles would be reasonable. Even could possibly connect here with the TC1 first act somehow, but in a way that the PCs would later move along with the 4th Crusade, eventually reaching Constantinople and fulfilling Bitter Crusade here, probably after spending some time in the city so the setting is familiar and feels more dramatic when facing the facts.<br /> <br /> From then, back to Central Europe after filling some time, to start Under the Black Cross, mostly as a sequel of Bitter Crusade, and to continue the remaining TC acts, having the PCs established some relationships previously to some main NPCs, and could have been requested join the Tzimisce revolt as having being abused (if they were) by their Sires or manipulated by other Elders. <br /> <br /> After completing that, beign reached by Cladius Giovanni for having being in touch with him previously, and also if their involvment in anarch revolts against elders is known, would be something reasonable as well, so they could be part of the Conspiracy of Isaac (depending on the outcome of past deeds, also could be reached by the Founders for taking the other side) so they start the Giovanni Chronicles from here.<br /> <br /> Not gotten into too much detail yet, but I was digging around to see if I could steal some ideas and that's how I found this really old topic...<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27473-duloc","name":"Duloc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T04:07:36-07:00","id":1535434,"title":"","content":"Greetings <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27473-duloc\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27473\" data-vbnamecard=\"27473\">Duloc</a> , scion of Cappadocius. Its not often we have a guest from the Clan of Death to grace these forums. <br /> <br /> Anyway I wish you the best of luck with both your chronicle and further practice with Mortis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T11:31:47-07:00","id":1535450,"title":"","content":"I've ran Giovanni Chronicles part 1 in Transylvania. With one coterie.<br /> <br /> I've ran Transylvania Chronicles part 1 and 2. Under the Black Cross (Magdeburg, Acre and Transylvania). I'm using heavily Dark Ages Europe and Transylvania By Night to fill in the gaps between the chapters (which are freaking huge gaping holes that the books do a poor job to cover). With another coterie.<br /> <br /> And I've played a solo game in Iberia using Clash of Wills and then Iberia By Night. The Storyteller took my PC then to Fountains of Bright Crimson (Jerusalem). <br /> <br /> Now I'm storytelling a homebrew campaign about a byzantine elder coterie going through the Holy Land coast to Jerusalem and then Alexandria. It's like a mini-crusade and Alexander campaign. But with a lot of diplomacy and intrigue instead of just military clash. It's has been very interesting, it's a solo game as well, with an Antonian Ventrue (controlled by my ex-Storyteller), a Lexor Brujah and a Draconian Tzimisce as NPCs. I'm using the fantastic Dark Ages Europe to make each city politics feel unique and offer a different challenge.<br /> Now we are going to Jerusalem, and I've studied Veil of the Night, Jerusalem by Night and Fountains of Bright Crimson.<br /> After it, I'm going to run Bitter Crusade as a continuation of this solo play. SO I'm also using Constantinople by Night.<br /> <br /> <br /> But, the book that has been the most help till now is Dark Ages Europe. It is very didactic and straight to the point, also creating in each region a network of geopolitics instead of creating a cast of characters to just showoff to your players. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}